VeridianOS: make invariants explicit (stringop, maybe-uninitialized)

Paths are relative to icu/source. One patch serves the host-tools build
(icu-host) and the target build (icu-cross); both reported the same
warnings, and both are clean with it.

- common/uresdata.cpp:1265 (ures_swapResource; reported in cmemory.h:68,
  uprv_memcpy) "specified bound between 18446744071562067968 and
  18446744073709551612 exceeds maximum object size
  [-Wstringop-overflow]": a URES_TABLE32 item count read from the bundle
  being swapped can be negative, and 4*count then converts to a huge
  size_t. In practice a negative count already failed later (in
  uprv_sortArray() or swapArray32(), with U_ILLEGAL_ARGUMENT_ERROR) before
  the memcpy, but nothing said so. The count is now validated where it is
  read: a negative count prints a udata error and fails with
  U_INVALID_FORMAT_ERROR, like ures_swap()'s other format checks. Valid
  bundles are unaffected.
- i18n/decNumber.cpp:2974 (uprv_decNumberSquareRoot) "writing 1 byte into
  a region of size 0 [-Wstringop-overflow]" (twice): with DECDPUN == 1 the
  initial approximation stored three digits with t->lsu[0..2]; t points
  into buft[D2N(3)], so the space exists, but the stores went through the
  one-element lsu[] member. The constants (t = 0.259/0.0819,
  a = 0.819/2.59) are now laid out with uprv_decNumberFromUInt32(), which
  writes through a Unit pointer and works for any DECDPUN, and the
  exponents are set after it; the three per-DECDPUN branches collapse into
  one. Same numbers: square roots of a sample of inputs at 30 digits are
  byte-identical before and after.
- i18n/number_mapper.cpp:135 (NumberPropertyMapper::oldToNew)
  "'currencyUsage' may be used uninitialized [-Wmaybe-uninitialized]": it
  was only assigned when useCurrency, and only read when
  properties.currencyUsage is set, which implies useCurrency. It is now
  initialized unconditionally with the same expression
  (properties.currencyUsage.getOrDefault(UCURR_USAGE_STANDARD)), which has
  no side effects. No behaviour change.
- tools/ctestfw/ctest.c:185 (createTestNode) "'strncpy' output truncated
  before terminating nul copying as many bytes from a string as its length
  [-Wstringop-truncation]": the code copies exactly nameLen characters of
  a longer or equal string and adds the NUL itself; it now says so with
  memcpy(). No behaviour change.


